# THE FOUR-TOWN CLUSTER RUN CONTINUED FROM ITS 100,000 CHECKPOINT WITH TWO TRAINING CHANGES (user 2026-11-15:
# "ok for 1 and 2", then "stop cluster training and use reward changes").
# = slurm/cluster_frl_c0actor_privcritic_4towns_ar2_keepgoal_nojx_fgx_lc01_miss_2m_par.env (job 466519, cancelled
#   at ~195,000 decisions: validation 43/80, 58/80, 43/80 at 75k/100k/150k, 70-98 m per fault throughout) with ONLY:
#   1. THE FAULT CHARGE 1 -> 50: a lane crossing, a collision or leaving the road costs 50 once and ends the
#      episode. It was 1 (crossing, collision) and 1 + 1 (off-road: the crossing charge plus
#      EXPLORE_OFF_ROAD_PENALTY, now 0 so every fault costs the same 50). Goal mode is paid the explore reward
#      plus +100 on arrival, so both modes change. Arriving pays +100 and 200 m of exploring pays +100.
#   2. THE TRAINING GOAL BAND 5-25 m -> 5-50 m. 85% of goals were already drawn past a junction (the ramp
#      reached 0.85 by 100,000; it restarts there, not at 0.5), so the change left is the distance.
# WHY: on Town07 hard with the uniform map 60 of 78 failures are a line crossed or the road left outside a
#   junction, 40 of the failures come at a turn, and both near-miss episodes cut the last corner at full lock.
# BOTH CHANGES ARE IN ONE RUN and were not tested apart (the local test of 1 alone was stopped at 2,000
#   decisions when the local card went to the map work); an effect cannot be assigned to either.
# Start with FRL_RESUME=<run>/step_100000 (the best validation checkpoint) under a NEW run name. A resume keeps
#   the learner and starts a fresh replay. Validation is unchanged (5-25 m, strict 1 m at <= 10 km/h).
. "$REPO/slurm/cluster_frl_c0actor_privcritic_4towns_ar2_keepgoal_nojx_fgx_lc01_miss_2m_par.env"
export LANE_DEPARTURE_PENALTY=50 LANE_COLLISION_PENALTY=50 EXPLORE_OFF_ROAD_PENALTY=0
export GOAL_DIST_MAX=50
export JUNCTION_RAMP_START=0.85
